From d3d5602278c6c9586ceb424ff5c4923605e02d16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: waxwing <ekaggata@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:21:33 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat: hash the trace as an authenticated jump list
 (opt-in)

With `jump_list: true` in the program definition, the step hash becomes
h(i) = BLAKE3(h(i-1) || h(jump(i)) || write_i || i)[..20], where jump(i)
is the long jump of S. D. Lerner's authenticated jump list ("Latest
innovations in BitVMX", June 2024), or i - 1 when step i has none. Any
step then reaches any earlier one in a few times log2(n) hops, so a
read's last write can be shown in one round instead of a second n-ary
search.

The executor keeps a table of the long jumps' targets (per data bit and
counter value), carried in checkpoints; the verifier checks a trace hash
against its own hash at the disputed step's long jump. Off by default:
the linear chain is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
